    {
      "turn": 1,
      "doctor_question": "Hello, I'm Dr. Smith. It's nice to meet you; could you tell me what brings you in to see me today?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S021",
      "patient_response": "Hi, Dr. Smith. Yeah, um... what brings me in is I just can't seem to keep my words in a straight line anymore. It's like... I'll start talking about an overnight shift. I work as an orderly, and the nights get really long, especially when it's quiet and you can just hear the vending machine humming down the hall. It makes this weird buzzing noise. But yeah, I'll try to tell someone about work, and suddenly I end up jumping to soccer. I played soccer back in high school, mostly on defense. Our jerseys were this really intense shade of blue. Which is funny, because the paint colors on the walls at the hospital are supposed to be calming, you know? Like this pale, washed-out green. But I'll be talking about the paint colors, and then suddenly I'm rambling about patient charts, and... I don't know, I just look at people's faces while I'm talking and I can see everyone getting completely lost. I just can't hold on to the point of what I'm trying to say.",
