    {
      "turn": 2,
      "doctor_question": "Beyond these difficulties with your speech, have you been experiencing any prolonged periods where your mood feels unusually elevated or, conversely, extremely low?",
      "targeted_symptom": "S024",
      "patient_response": "Yeah, um... low. Extremely low. Most days I just feel so heavy and completely empty right from the time I wake up. It's hard to even get moving. Like, after my shifts at the hospital, I'll just sit out in my car crying for a long time before I can even bring myself to drive home. I usually park in the employee lot, near the back by the dumpsters, because the front row fills up so fast by the time I get there. The seagulls always hang around those dumpsters. It's weird because we're not even that close to the ocean, but there are always seagulls out there. They make that awful screeching sound. I tried throwing them a piece of a granola bar once, the oats and honey kind, but they didn't even want it. They just want the garbage. I used to eat those granola bars every single day in high school. My locker was right next to the cafeteria doors, so it always smelled like tater tots... wait, what did you ask me? About my mood? Yeah, just... crying in my car. Really empty.",
