    {
      "turn": 4,
      "doctor_question": "Have you ever had a period of time where you felt unusually energetic, didn't need much sleep, or felt like your thoughts were racing, even if you weren't feeling sad?",
      "targeted_symptom": null,
      "patient_response": "No, um... no, I've never really felt like that. I'm pretty much always just exhausted. I don't think I've ever had a time where I didn't need sleep. I'm usually trying to get more sleep, especially because the coffee in the breakroom at work is so terrible. They have this machine that uses those little plastic pods, but whoever does the ordering keeps getting the decaf ones with the orange foil on top. I don't know why anyone would want decaf on a night shift. But orange is just... it's a really loud color, you know? Like those traffic cones they set up when they do road work on the highway. The reflective tape on them always catches my headlights when I'm driving home in the dark. My car's headlights are actually getting kind of dim, I think I need to replace the bulbs soon. But you have to take the whole front bumper off just to get to the plastic housing for the bulb, which is such a stupid design. My uncle used to be a mechanic and he'd always complain about how cars are built these days, how everything is just cheap plastic clips that snap off if you pull them wrong... um... but yeah, no. I don't get energetic or have racing thoughts like that. I just sleep whenever I can.",
